wise pr:escribed by this Act, all decisions of the tsoard ofGovernor-s shall be taken on the basis of the opinion of a majority of .the memberspresent. ln the event of the rnembers being evenly divided on any matter theperson presiding over the meeting shall have a casting vote.(tO) The quorum for a meeting of the Board of Governors shall be two thirds ofits rnembership, a fr.action being counted as one.::22, ow rs a i ns o he id of GovErnbrs.- (l)The Board ofGovernors.,shall have the power of general supervision over the lnstitute and shallhold the Vice=Chancellor and the Authorities accountable for all the functions ofthe Institute. The Board of Covernors shall have all powers of the 'lnstitute not
